  "Question": "Which of the following polynomials can be factored using the difference of squares formula?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-x^2+y^2\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^2+y^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(-x^2-y^2\\)",
    "D": "\\(x^2-2y\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(-x^2+y^2=y^2-x^2=(y+x)(y-x)\\). The difference of squares requires 2 terms with opposite signs, each of which is a square.",
